$2x-3=0$ gives $x=\dfrac{3}{2}$, with multiplicity $2$, so the curve touches the $x$-axis at $\left(\dfrac{3}{2},0\right)$ and turns back.
$x=-1$ has multiplicity $1$, so the curve cuts straight through at $(-1,0)$.

